# Copy to .ppprc (git-ignored) and adjust for your machine.
# These are the flags your build/std.pcm must have been built with —
# if you change them, run ./ppp std again.

# ── macOS with Homebrew LLVM (Apple's clang can't do `import std;` yet) ──
# LLVM="$(brew --prefix llvm)"
# CXX="$LLVM/bin/clang++"
# EXTRA_LDFLAGS="-L$LLVM/lib/c++ -Wl,-rpath,$LLVM/lib/c++"

# ── Debian/Ubuntu (apt.llvm.org or distro clang + libc++-N-dev) ──
# Usually nothing needed: ./ppp std finds std.cppm next to clang++.
# Only if plain `clang++` isn't the version you set up:
# CXX=clang++-21
# STD_CPPM=/usr/lib/llvm-21/share/libc++/v1/std.cppm

# STD_FLAGS="-std=c++23 -stdlib=libc++"
# WARN_FLAGS="-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion -Wshadow -g"
